The first defense says the same class of check would have caught LiteLLM's untagged PyPI uploads. The four topics are the page's related defense topics.
notes:
The page's text links one other kill chain, and the page lists four defense topics.

In its first defense, the page says that checking released artifacts correspond to the commits they claim is the same class of check that would have caught LiteLLM's untagged PyPI uploads. That incident has its own kill chain. PyPI is the Python Package Index. The page draws no other connection between the two.

The related defense topics are CI/CD and supply chain, vulnerability management, container security, and threat modeling. CI/CD stands for continuous integration and continuous delivery.
